<%# GET /thecyberpulse/bio — the long-form record as a console screen
    (2026-10-29; the seven stacked glowing fieldsets are gone): the XERAEN
    bio's twin — a bar, "// SECTION //" rules, 16/20 prose, the newest VOD
    embedded under // VISUAL TRANSMISSION // (as the fieldset page had),
    THE PULSE GRID readouts as status rows, the closing quote, destination
    rows and the "> " prompt. data-boot="done" + autofocus off: no line
    reveal, and the prompt never steals the keyboard from scrolling.
    bio-credit replays the bio_viewed achievement POST for logged-in
    viewers. Assigns: @latest_vod, @vod_video_id. %>
<% content_for :title, "The.CyberPul.se Bio — hackr.tv" %>
<% current_year = Date.current.year %>
<% future_year = current_year + 100 %>

<%= render layout: "shared/default_chrome", locals: {ascii: false} do %>
  <div class="console console--thecyberpulse xt-bio" data-controller="terminal bio-credit" data-boot="done"
       data-terminal-autofocus-value="false" data-bio-credit-slug-value="thecyberpulse">
    <div class="console-bar">
      <h1 class="console-bar-title">THE.CYBERPUL.SE</h1>
      <span class="console-bar-sub">OPERATIVE RECORD · BIO</span>
      <span class="console-bar-right">
        <%= link_to "[<] TCP", "/thecyberpulse", class: "console-bar-link" %>
        <%= link_to "[>] RELEASES", "/thecyberpulse/releases", class: "console-bar-link" %>
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// SIGNAL INCOMING //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p class="xt-lead">You're not supposed to be hearing this.</p>
      <p><%= codex_text("This frequency shouldn't exist. This transmission is being broadcast from a timeline [[GovCorp]] has spent a century trying to prevent. And yet - here we are. Here ") %><em>you</em> are. Listening.</p>
      <p><%= codex_text("The.CyberPul.se is the central nervous system of the [[The Fracture Network|Fracture Network]]. Not a band. Not a channel. A heartbeat transmitted backward through time from #{future_year} to #{current_year} — a hundred years of truth compressed into electromagnetic pulses you're decoding right now.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-brand">Welcome to hackr.tv. The signal is live. The Pulse is strong.</p>
    </div>

    <% if @latest_vod && @vod_video_id %>
      <div class="console-rule"><span>// VISUAL TRANSMISSION //</span></div>
      <div class="tcp-embed">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<%= @vod_video_id %>"
                title="<%= @latest_vod.title.presence || "Visual transmission" %>"
                allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
                allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
      <% if @latest_vod.title.present? %>
        <p class="xt-tuning"><%= @latest_vod.title %></p>
      <% end %>
      <div class="console-row">
        <span class="console-tag">[VIDZ]</span>
        <%= link_to "The archive", "/thecyberpulse/vidz", class: "console-link" %>
        <span class="console-desc">Every broadcast on record — all the visual transmissions</span>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE BROADCAST //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p class="xt-lead">24/7. No dead air. No corporate sponsorship. No holding back.</p>
      <p><%= codex_text("What you'll find here: multiple [[Fracture Network]] bands transmitting their frequencies through our broadcast. Live operations against [[GovCorp]] infrastructure. Interactive coordination through [[THE PULSE GRID]]. A community of listeners who've become operators, viewers who've become fighters, audience members who've realized they were always part of the show.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-brand">This isn't entertainment. This is a recruitment broadcast disguised as a streaming platform.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE HOSTS //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] XERAEN</h3>
      <p><%= codex_text("He broadcasts from #{future_year} - from a future where [[GovCorp]] has won, where [[rainns|RAINNs]] have replaced authentic human expression, where [[The Fracture Network]] fights a war most people don't know is happening.") %></p>
      <p><%= codex_text("[[XERAEN]] sends transmissions backward through time. Not to warn you. Not to save you. To ") %><em>activate</em> you.</p>
      <p>
        Every transmission you receive has already happened in his timeline. Every attack you witness
        is history to him - but to you, it's still possible. Still changeable. The paradox is the point:
        he's broadcasting from a future he's trying to prevent.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-dim"><%= codex_text("If [[The Fracture Network]] succeeds, XERAEN's timeline collapses. He ceases to exist. The broadcasts stop because there's nothing left to broadcast from.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-brand">He fights knowing victory means erasure.</p>

      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] RYKER M. PULSE</h3>
      <p class="xt-lead">If XERAEN carries the signal, Ryker is the heartbeat.</p>
      <p>
        Co-founder. Primary drummer. The voice that cuts through static and demands you <em>move</em>.
        While XERAEN works the code and maintains the transmission, Ryker brings the kinetic energy
        that turns broadcasts into rallying cries.
      </p>
      <p>
        His drums don't keep time - they <em>drive</em> it. Every beat is a countdown. Every rhythm is
        a call to action. When Ryker's voice comes through the broadcast, it's not a whisper from the
        future. It's a shout. A challenge. A reminder that resistance isn't passive.
      </p>
      <p>XERAEN sends the transmission. Ryker makes sure it hits like a fist.</p>
      <p>
        Where XERAEN embodies the solitary weight of maintaining hope across impossible distances,
        Ryker embodies defiance made physical. Unity through action. The belief that every small choice
        ripples forward - or in their case, backward - shaping futures that haven't been written yet.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-dim">
        He knows the math. He knows that success means erasure. He drums anyway. Louder. Faster.
        Like he's trying to leave dents in the timeline itself.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-brand">Some people whisper about change. Ryker beats it into existence.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE PULSE GRID //</span></div>
    <div class="console-status">
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">CONNECTION</span><span class="console-val">ACTIVE</span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">NODES</span><span class="console-val">EXPANDING</span></div>
      <div class="console-status-row"><span class="console-key">STATUS</span><span class="console-val"><span class="xt-brand">SYNCHRONIZED</span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p><%= codex_text("It's not a game. [[THE PULSE GRID]] is how [[the Fracture Network]] coordinates across timelines - a MUD interface where operators train, plan, and execute. What looks like a text adventure is actually FN infrastructure.") %></p>
      <p><%= codex_text("Every zone corresponds to real [[GovCorp]] territory. Every puzzle mirrors actual security protocols. Every player who masters the grid becomes capable of navigating its real-world equivalent.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-brand">You thought you were playing. You were preparing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// WHAT WE TRANSMIT //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] THE BANDS</h3>
      <p><%= codex_text("Over 10 frequencies. More than a dozen approaches to [[GovCorp]] resistance. From Injection Vector's kinetic warfare to Ethereality's oceanic depth - each band represents a node in the network, a tactic in the arsenal, a way of fighting that speaks to different souls.") %></p>
      <p class="xt-dim">
        We don't tell you which frequency to tune to. We broadcast them all. You find the frequency that
        resonates with your resistance.
      </p>
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] THE OPERATIONS</h3>
      <p><%= codex_text("Live attacks against [[The RIDE|GovCorp systems]]. Real-time infiltration of corporate infrastructure. Interactive missions where the audience doesn't just watch - they participate. Every livestream is an operation. Every viewer is potentially an operator.") %></p>
      <h3 class="xt-sub">[+] THE FREQUENCY</h3>
      <p>
        Purple light cutting through their manufactured darkness. A frequency they can't jam because
        it's not coming from anywhere they can locate. We exist in the space between their surveillance
        systems, in the temporal gap their algorithms can't process.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-dim">They know we're broadcasting. They just can't figure out <em>when</em> we're broadcasting from.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// THE PARADOX //</span></div>
    <div class="xt-prose">
      <p>Here's why we're GovCorp's nightmare:</p>
      <p>
        If they stop us in <%= future_year %>, the broadcasts have already been sent to <%= current_year %>. If they stop
        the listeners in <%= current_year %>, the resistance in <%= future_year %> has already formed. We exist in both
        timelines simultaneously - a transmission that's already arrived and a future that hasn't happened yet.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-brand">Causality bent. We broadcast through the fracture.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-rule"><span>// LAST WORDS //</span></div>
    <blockquote class="xt-quote">
      <p>You found this signal for a reason.</p>
      <p class="xt-quote-gap">
        You're hearing this broadcast because somewhere in the electromagnetic spectrum between <%= current_year %> and <%= future_year %>,
        your frequency matched ours.
      </p>
      <p class="xt-quote-gap">The Pulse is strong. The signal is live. The network is expanding.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="xt-sig">Broadcasting to the past to stop the future of today. <span class="console-dim">· Welcome to The.CyberPul.se.</span></p>

    <%= render "artist_pages/console_destinations", artist: "thecyberpulse", except: "BIO" %>
    <%= render "shared/console_prompt", hint: console_prompt_hint("thecyberpulse", except: "BIO") %>
  </div>
<% end %>
